          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.845,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "to be detailed enough so that one can physically construct the objects they depict."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.126,
            0.772,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We will now explore some ways of drawing solids on a plane."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.156,
            0.278,
            0.175
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Projections"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.18,
            0.846,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The net of a solid (when it exists) is one way of representing a solid on the plane. But it can be difficult to visualise the solid from the net, without physically cutting out the net and folding it up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.236,
            0.847,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Another way to represent a solid is by looking at the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "projections",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of all its points on a plane. This idea is closely related to the profile of a solid from a specific viewpoint, which we discussed earlier. Let us see how this technique works."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.348,
            0.307,
            0.666,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.348,
                0.307,
                0.666,
                0.53
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_18_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.548,
            0.845,
            0.585
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider a point P in space, and a plane M. Imagine a line from P intersecting the plane M at a point O."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.585,
            0.847,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We say that OP is "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "perpendicular to the plane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " if for any line OX on the plane, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle POX = 90^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In this case, we say that point O is the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "projection",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of point P on the plane. The projections of all the points of an object together form the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "projection of the object on the plane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.669,
            0.534,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Let us visualise the projection of a line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.185,
            0.691,
